Package: bayesval
Title: Bayesian Probabilistic Validation of Cox Prediction Models
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Willem M.", "Otte", email = "w.m.otte@umcutrecht.nl",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-1511-6834")),
    person("Sem L.", "Kampman", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-2093-9389")))
Description: Turns the standard discrimination/calibration validation of Cox
    proportional-hazards models into a fully Bayesian, probabilistic procedure:
    every validation quantity (Harrell/Uno/Gonen-Heller/Antolini concordance,
    time-dependent AUC, calibration-in-the-large, slope, ICI/E50/E90,
    D-calibration, IPCW Brier/IBS/IPA, R2_D, and decision-curve net benefit) is
    reported as a posterior distribution with a credible interval. A single
    estimation principle (evaluate any existing frequentist estimator at each
    posterior draw) propagates model-parameter uncertainty; the Bayesian
    bootstrap adds evaluation-sample uncertainty; calibration is assessed by a
    posterior predictive check.
